From: guillermo <guillermo.karsz@solid-run.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Sep 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ddr: add a SolidRun SOM DDR configuration node (v1.11 values)

Hailo BSP 1.12.0 rewrote the shared LPDDR4 register tables (base table and
per-part patch) with values tuned on Hailo's boards. On the SolidRun
Hailo-15 SOM the 1.12 values are not stable under sustained memory load
(one byte lane intermittently reads zeros, kernel panics after minutes);
the v1.11 values, equal to the configuration the SOM was validated with,
are stable (4.5 h of verified stress testing).

Instead of modifying Hailo's tables, use the SCU's per-part patch
mechanism: add a SolidRun-owned patch node in the board device tree that
lists every register where the v1.11 configuration differs from the
v1.12.1 base table (125 registers), and select it via assembled_dram_pn.
Hailo's files stay untouched; the node is generated from Hailo's tables
and is the place for SOM-specific DDR tuning in the future.

---
--- a/arch/arm/dts/hailo15-solidrun.dts	2026-09-10 07:32:03.232220798 +0000
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/hailo15-solidrun.dts	2026-09-10 07:32:03.233766239 +0000
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include "hailo15-base.dtsi"
 #include "hailo15_ddr_configuration.dtsi"
 #include "hailo1x_ddr_MT53E1G32D2FW-046-B_regconfig_ca_odtb_pd_4GB_LP4.dtsi"
+#include "hailo15-solidrun-ddr.dtsi"
 #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
 
 / {
--- /dev/null	2026-09-08 07:05:11.610637491 +0000
